    "answer": {
      "short": "$15\\text{ cm}$; $\\sqrt{12^2+9^2}=15$.",
      "worked": "The diagonals of a rhombus bisect each other at right angles, forming four right-angled triangles. Each triangle has perpendicular sides of $24\\div2=12\\text{ cm}$ and $18\\div2=9\\text{ cm}$. Each rhombus side is a hypotenuse. By Pythagoras’ theorem,\n$$\\begin{align*}l^2&=12^2+9^2\\\\l^2&=144+81\\\\l^2&=225\\\\l&=\\sqrt{225}\\\\l&=15\\text{ cm}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
